{
  "version": 2,
  "about": [
    "The machine-readable half of each handoff skill: how to invoke that harness through its supported SDK/protocol route or CLI fallback.",
    "This file and skills-src/ are the single source of truth; the fourteen",
    "<harness>-harness-handoff/ trees are generated from them by scripts/build_skills.py.",
    "",
    "Contract version 2 preserves the pinned CLI fallback while adding a required sdk object. SDK routes are preferred only where the sdk object authorizes them; CLI argv remains the fallback. A continuation value of forbidden means the route is policy-prohibited even if the underlying product can technically do it.",
    "",
    "harness-fleet's adapters cite these skills as their execution contract (see the module",
    "docstring in harness_fleet/providers/<harness>.py). scripts/check_harness_drift.py in",
    "the harness-fleet checkout validates each adapter against this file, so a change here",
    "that the adapters do not match fails a check instead of silently diverging.",
    "",
    "Placeholders in oneshot_argv: <prompt> is the prompt text, <model> the route model,",
    "<workspace> the call workspace, <prompt-file> the staged prompt file, and <workdir>",
    "the adapter's per-call temporary directory (codex writes <workdir>/final.md).",
    "",
    "interactivity declares the approval posture of the pinned oneshot argv:",
    "non_interactive configures approvals away and never parks; prompts can reach an",
    "approval boundary, where the host parks an explicit awaiting-approval receipt.",
    "credential_channel and credential_auth declare how the harness reaches its own",
    "credentials (env | stdin | file | keychain | native-session); the pinned argv",
    "passes no credential values, so these name how per-invocation grants reach the",
    "harness when it is host-managed, and the harness's native auth otherwise."
  ],
  "placeholders": ["<prompt>", "<model>", "<workspace>", "<prompt-file>", "<workdir>"],
  "advisory_vocabulary": {
    "status": ["started", "milestone", "blocked", "done"],
    "fan_out": ["blocked", "done"],
    "semantics": "self-reported presence, never proof of completion; carries no control state and never blocks the lane",
    "implemented_by": "work-coordination"
  },
  "harnesses": {
